 darkroomTitle:'From negative to print.',darkroomLead:'A private, guided, four-hour analogue printing course in a small darkroom. Choose a frame, make a test strip and watch your own black-and-white photograph appear on paper.',duration:'Duration',level:'Level',beginners:'Beginners welcome',group:'Group',fourHours:'4 hours',privateSession:'Private session',privateAdults:'1–2 adults',familyOption:'Family option',familyValue:'Up to 2 adults and 2 children aged 12+',courseTitle:'The Darkroom — A hands-on course',courseIntro:'Discover the art of analogue printing in an intimate, hands-on darkroom session. Learn how to transform your negatives into photographs using light, chemistry and traditional silver gelatin printing.',courseIntro2:'The session is designed for beginners, with individual guidance throughout the process, from selecting a negative to exposing, developing and washing your final print.',courseSub:'A private learning experience',courseList:['Up to 2 adults','Families welcome: up to 2 adults and 2 children aged 12+','4-hour guided session','No previous experience needed','Materials included'],courseClose:'You’ll learn at your own pace, experiment with light and contrast, and create your own handmade prints to take home.',included:'Included',darkroomIncluded:'Paper, chemistry and darkroom equipment',darkroomIntro:'Bring developed black-and-white negatives. If your film still needs processing, arrange that before the workshop.',processTitle:'The process, in six steps',printSteps:['Choose a negative on the light table.','Place the negative in the enlarger and focus.','Use a test strip to choose the exposure.','Expose the photographic paper.','Develop, stop and fix the print.','Wash, dry and look at what you made.'],learnTitle:'Learn by making a print.',learnText:'Focus, exposure, contrast and paper. You work through each part of the process with guidance, then take your finished silver gelatin prints home.',darkroomNote:'This is a printing course. Club F/65 is a separate day of photographing outdoors and developing sheet film.',bring:'What to bring',bringText:'Developed black-and-white negatives, a few frames you would like to print and closed shoes. We provide the darkroom materials.',darkroomFaq:[['I have never used a darkroom. Is this for me?','Yes. The session starts with the equipment and the process, then moves to your own print.'],['Can I come without a camera?','Yes. You need developed negatives for the printing session. You can rent a camera and arrange film developing beforehand.'],['Do I take my prints home?','Yes, once they are washed and dry.']],bookSession:'Book a darkroom session',
